    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-celsus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very high</i>
			or <i>lofty</i> (class.; <b>poet.</b>
			and late Lat.; cf.: arduus, sublimis, excelsus). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rupes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 245</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev. Chron. 2, 15,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fortuna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 3, 3, 85</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp.</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ambros. Fid. 4, 1, 7</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. in Luc. 3, 3, 37</span></i> (but
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 48, § 107</span></i>,
			perexcelso, B. and K.).</div>
